      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I could reproduce.\n\nSelecting multiple objects break custom trigger target values of some VRChat component in Unity editor. It will occur on VRC_MidiNoteIn, VRC_AudioBank and VRC_OscButtonIn.\n\n (It doesn't occur on VRC_Station because multiple objects editing is not supported by its custom editor. VRC_DestructibleStandard has trigger definition, but that are different format.)\n\nFor dev:\nThis is problem of CustomTriggerTargetDrawer in VRC_TriggerEditor.cs\nThese pages would be helpful.\n https://gamedev.stackexchange.com/questions/122301/how-can-i-create-a-custom-propertydrawer-for-my-point-struct/123609#123609\n https://answers.unity.com/questions/1214493/custompropertydrawer-cant-restrict-multi-editing.html\nI think we need BeginProperty - BeginChangeCheck - EndChangeCheck - EndProperty pattern for each properly inside VRCSDK2.VRC_Trigger.CustomTriggerTarget",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
